        "fields": {
          "notes": "Work identity follows the current GND work authority. The documentary route now distinguishes region-only preparatory evidence in W II notebooks; the D 22 / GSA 71/29 print manuscript; the independent Overbeck NL 53 : A 311 copy; the editorially intervened Koegel/Naumann 1895 first print; the source-visible 1906 Naumann collection member; later de-suppressed and critical layers; and eKGWB addresses without admitting any remote text body. The proposed Gesetz wider das Christenthum route remains a separate contested associated adjunct at GSA 71/32 fol. 47, not AC 63 and not part of the D 22 object. The provisional Russian translation remains a separate expression."
        },
